---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main
    class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center min-h-screen text-white font-mono px-6 py-16 text-center"
  >
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl mb-8 animate-fade-in-slow">My Why</h1>

    <p
      class="max-w-3xl text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed animate-fade-in-slow opacity-80"
    >
      Memory is the most <strong class="text-indigo-300"
        >idiosyncratic, humanistic</strong
      > aspect in us. It is the story that we keep telling ourselves about who we
      are, why we do things the way we do, and how it shapes the person we’re becoming.
      It’s <strong class="text-indigo-300">hauntingly beautiful</strong> and sometimes&nbsp;
      <strong class="text-indigo-300">painfully poetic</strong>, but most
      importantly, it’s <strong class="text-indigo-300"
        >innately prevalent</strong
      > in our everyday life. To me, memory is what gives life <strong
        class="text-indigo-300"><em>"meaning"</em></strong
      >. How can something so abstract, so difficult to conceptualize, be so
      ingrained in our identity? Clearly, we don’t know much about ourselves as
      we let on.
    </p>

    <p
      class="max-w-3xl mt-8 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed animate-fade-in-slow opacity-80"
    >
      What continues to fascinate me is the question of what makes us <strong
        class="text-indigo-300"><em>truly us</em></strong
      >. Not just through intellectual frameworks, but also through humanistic
      perspectives because <strong class="text-indigo-300"
        ><em>both are connected and part of the same system</em></strong
      >.
    </p>

    <p
      class="max-w-3xl mt-10 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed animate-fade-in-slow opacity-75"
    >
      As Jill Bolte Taylor said, <strong class="text-indigo-300"
        ><em
          >"Most of us think of ourselves as thinking creatures that feel, but
          we are actually feeling creatures that think."</em
        ></strong
      >
    </p>
  </main>

  <style>
    .animate-fade-in-slow {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(20px);
      animation: floatFade 2.2s ease forwards;
    }

    @keyframes floatFade {
      to {
        opacity: 0.8;
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
    }

    html,
    body {
      min-height: 100%;
      margin: 0;
      overflow-y: auto;
    }

    body::-webkit-scrollbar {
      display: none;
    }

    body {
      -ms-overflow-style: none;
      scrollbar-width: none;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
